  "limitations": [
    "Finite range model is one attempt after validated metadata while data is protected; no mechanical refinement of the full Rust I/O/copy loop, concurrency, retry composition or recovery.",
    "The probe is a measurement harness, not Verus-proved production code; independent Python checks cover full small-workload chunk hashes and remote request prefixes/suffixes.",
    "100 GB is real payload I/O; no new physical TB or sparse-TB evidence.",
    "The source regenerates position-dependent data in 1 MiB callback pieces. Publication excludes separately reported checksum preparation but includes regeneration/hashing/write/sync; it is not a raw-filesystem bandwidth measurement.",
    "Whole read-workflow timing includes SSH, oracle comparison and additional small-slice scans. Native-call times exclude the subsequent oracle; checked bytes are logical payload authentication, not physical backend I/O.",
    "No cache eviction, CPU isolation or hard latency/bandwidth SLA. TLC/Verus ran on the writer host. Samples mix positions and are not independent.",
    "All data was normally collected before removing private metadata directories and remote binaries. GC namespace deletion does not measure backend object-reclamation completion.",
    "An error-free observation is not a claim that straw has no remaining bugs or proof gaps."
  ],
